# Real-Postgres coverage for FR12's enforcement half (task #2097, plan
# #2080): fresh host-port allocation outside the server's configured
# allowed ranges must refuse on the same synchronous failure path as a
# port conflict (PortOutOfRangeError), ranges constrain only their
# protocol, a range-less server stays unconstrained (SB-1.2), and a range
# change leaves existing allocations intact while binding the next fresh
# one (OQ5). Gated behind `//go:build integration`, gazelle skips it when
# scanning for go_test srcs; hand-written with the EXACT tag set from
# //libs/go/dbtest:postgres_constraints_test.
#
# Run it explicitly (requires a working Docker daemon):
#   bazel test //manmanv2/api/repository/postgres:server_port_enforcement_integration_test --test_output=all
go_test(
